# Fallow after code generation

After you generate, edit, or delete code — and before you say the task is done — run:

```bash
npx fallow dead-code --format json
```

If the change is on a branch, `npx fallow audit` is enough: it only looks at files this branch changed.

Do not add `fallow` as a project dependency unless asked. `npx` is enough.

## What to fix

Fix findings this change introduced: unused exports, unused types, unused files you just added.

```ts
// BAD — exported "for later", nothing imports it
export const dimensionSchema = z.enum(["input", "output"]);

// GOOD — keep it in the file, export when a second caller needs it
const dimensionSchema = z.enum(["input", "output"]);
```

## What to leave

Do not delete or suppress pre-existing noise without asking:

- shadcn/ui kit exports (`CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, …) that later pages will use
- CLI scripts under `scripts/` that are run with `pnpm`/`tsx`, not imported
- packages Fallow cannot see as imports (`shadcn` CLI, Tailwind plugins)
